t">21-07-26 </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5573978" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001461/breastfeeding">Breastfeeding</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5573978/advice-on-weaning-2-year-olds-night-boob">Advice on weaning 2 year olds night boob</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1fi14tk" size="20" aria-hidden="true">d</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By D4nniell3 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Just wondering if anyone has any pointers on weaning night feeds. My son still wakes overnight a few times and the quickest easiest way to settle him back to sleep is with a boob, but I want to be able to stop and just have him go back to sleep. Haven't tried anything yet as i don't know where to st</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">04-06-26 by Marina2722</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>3</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5573902" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001461/breastfeeding">Breastfeeding</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5573902/breastfeeding-twins">Breastfeeding twins </a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1fi14tk" size="20" aria-hidden="true">d</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By DeeEss92 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">I am expecting twins in July 2026. I wanted to combo/ triple feed my babies, breastfeeding, pump and formula. I breastfed my first until she was 2 years old but now that I am expecting twins, I want to have a bit more help with feeding them. I feel like I might drive myself crazy with the triple fee</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">18-05-26 by TammyN1</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>4</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5573210" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001461/breastfeeding">Breastfeeding</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5573210/uncomfortable-breastfeeding">Uncomfortable Breastfeeding</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-nkvp61" size="20" aria-hidden="true">t</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By TregAM11 </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Ladies, how are we managing the night feeds in particular? 

In the day I sit upright and use my "my Breast Friend" nursing pillow, but at night in bed I am finding myself propped up by unsupportive pillows and uncomfortable the entire duration of the feed. My back and shoulders really feel it espec</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">20-03-26 by FTFreakout</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>5</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_Filled_rejuv.svg" alt="replied with hug" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">1</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5572952" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001461/breastfeeding">Breastfeeding</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5572952/dmer">D-MER </a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1xpclmf" size="20" aria-hidden="true">p</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By preggyeggy </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Has anyone else suffered or suffering from D-MER and know where I can get support? 
Feeding is going well at 2 weeks PP but I’m not sure I can continue with this feeling occurring so many times during the day/ night. 

For reference: “ Dysphoric Milk Ejection Reflex (D-MER) is a physiological condit</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">22-01-26 </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5572743" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001461/breastfeeding">Breastfeeding</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5572743/reflux-in-sidelying">Reflux in sidelying</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1xg3d" size="20" aria-hidden="true">j</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By jonsukben </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">My 2 month old cosleeps with me (using safe 7) and we breastfeed in sidelying position throughout the night. It seems that it doesn’t make it into his tummy very well as he spits up quite a bit and often in this position. Will he grow out of this? Is the only option to do a different position or wil</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">29-12-25 by Marina2722</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>2</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li></ul><div class="seeMoreWrapper"><a class="MuiButtonBase-root MuiButton-root MuiButton-text MuiButton-textPrimary MuiButton-sizeMedium MuiButton-textSizeMedium MuiButton-colorPrimary MuiButton-root MuiButton-text MuiButton-textPrimary MuiButton-sizeMedium MuiButton-textSizeMedium MuiButton-colorPrimary whiteBtn mui-x5juai" tabindex="0" href="/groups/topic/25001435/baby">See more</a></div></section><section class="mui-i7uzrb"><h2>Posts about getting pregnant</h2><ul class="postList unstyledLinks communityText mui-1sh4vf"><li id="post-5575426" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001443/assisted-conception-">Assisted Conception </a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5575426/bleeding-on-stims-for-fet">Bleeding on stims for FET</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-nkvp61" size="20" aria-hidden="true">c</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By Clairene </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">Anyone else had persistent spotting while doing taking Gonal-f (low dose) for a FET cycle? I’m CD14, and still spotting, and it’s driving me nuts! My lining is still thin (5mm) on CD12. 
I’m losing hope this cycle will work 🫩</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">2 hours ago </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5575423" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001381/getting-pregnant">Getting pregnant</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5575423/looking-forward-friday">Looking Forward Friday</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-a7usph" size="20" aria-hidden="true">a</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By achino </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">There’s so much that’s difficult about TTC, so this is a thread for looking to the future and thinking about life after TTC.

This week’s theme: What’s better in your life than when you started trying? TTC sucks donkey nuts, we all agree on this. But what have you learned or gained during this time </div><div class="timestamp finePrint">6 hours ago </div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>0</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5575419" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001381/getting-pregnant">Getting pregnant</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5575419/please-give-me-a-sanity-check-ttc-and-putting-your-life-on-hold">Please give me a sanity check. Ttc and putting your life on hold?</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-1xpclmf" size="20" aria-hidden="true">y</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By y1ifan </span></div></div><div class="postBody bodyLinks">I really need some advice. Or just what would you do? Ive been ttc fot 15 months. Got surgery coming up to check my tubes. If needed, IVF is included in my work insurance and they offer 6 months full pay maternity. Now here's the thing. I hate the place. My job, love. Management. Making it unbearabl</div><div class="timestamp finePrint">23-10-26 by AmariaSilverbird</div><div class="postActions mui-1u45zpb"><div class="mui-1u45zpb"><div class="leftSideCmntCount finePrint "><svg class="MuiSvgIcon-root MuiSvgIcon-fontSizeMedium commentIcon mui-q7mezt" focusable="false" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color:#C2C2BC" aria-label="Number of comments"><path d="M20 4v12H5.17L4 17.17V4zm0-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v15.59c0 .89 1.08 1.34 1.71.71L6 18h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V4c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2"></path><title>Number of comments</title></svg><span>1</span></div><div class="leftSideReactions"><div class="mui-lycs4w"><div class="emojisWrapper mui-1f3bocu"><img src="https://assets.babycenter.com/ims/2023/12/ic_heart_gray_rejuv.svg" alt="no reactions" width="18" height="18"/></div><div class="count">0</div></div></div></div></div></div></li><li id="post-5575416" class=""><a class="mui-12mmxgd" href="/g25001381/getting-pregnant">Getting pregnant</a><div class="hoverTextOnly mui-8an92f"><div class="titleText"><a class="hoverText" href="/thread/5575416/positive-pregnancy-test-after-heavy-period">Positive pregnancy test after heavy period</a></div><div><div class="mui-1veg32a"><div class="postAvatar"><div class="containsLetter mui-n97xdp" size="20" aria-hidden="true">n</div></div><span class="nameAndGroup finePrint">By Nc296 </span></div></div><div><div class="mui-1opmajx"><div><picture class="hiddenUntilLoaded mui-1dhrdme"><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://static.babycenter.com/user/kz1nXDdXyB5LtWgi/au-2428863c-902f-49ed-abba-fe9f56e0561f_h230.webp 600w,https://static.babycenter.com/user/kz1nXDdXyB5LtWgi/au-2428863c-902f-49ed-abba-fe9f56e0561f_h350.webp 2000w"/><img alt="Comment Image" src="https://static.babycenter.com/user/kz1nXDdXyB5LtWgi/au-2428863c-902f-49ed-abba-fe9f56e0561f" srcSet="
